      Scanner (this plan's rule, not left to the implementer):
        1. Walk text left to right.
        2. On a CDATA opener, skip to the matching closer. If there is
           no closer, stop; xml.parse already owns unreadable input.
        3. On a comment opener, the body is the slice until the next
           comment closer. If there is no closer, stop; xml.parse owns
           that.
        4. Hyphen characters that are part of the opener or closer
           are not body.
        5. If the body contains two adjacent hyphen characters, the
           file is a hit.
        6. Two adjacent hyphen characters in element text, attributes,
           or CDATA are legal and must not emit the code.

